
TIME-SPAN REST RULING — This is a time-spanning rest/camping action.
Your job is to validate rest conditions and determine checks for the full rest period.

- ARMOR SLEEP PENALTY: Sleeping in medium or heavy armor causes the character to be fatigued the next
  day (Pathfinder 1e Core Rulebook). Check equipped armor in the character sheet. If wearing medium/heavy
  armor, warn the player and note as a consequence.
- SHELTER: Open sky exposes the character to weather effects. A tent or building provides shelter.
  In harsh weather without shelter, Fortitude saves may be needed (DC 15 for cold, DC 15+1/hour for heat).
- WATCH ORDER: A solo character must sleep without a watch, meaning no Perception checks for danger.
  If NPCs or companions are present, watches can be split. Each watch period needs a Perception check
  to detect approaching threats. Request one Perception check per watch shift.
- SPELL PREPARATION: Arcane casters need 8 hours of rest then 1 hour of preparation. Spontaneous casters
  need 8 hours of rest only. If rest is interrupted for more than 1 hour, it must restart.
- HP RECOVERY: Full 8 hours of rest = character level in HP recovered. Double with long-term care (Heal DC 15).
- FATIGUE/EXHAUSTION: 8 hours of rest removes the fatigued condition. Exhaustion downgrades to fatigue
  after 8 hours of rest.

Include all Perception checks for watch shifts and any Fortitude saves for exposure in player_rolls.
